@title Preparing for your MRI scan
@subtitle St. Anselm Imaging, patient instructions

Most people have an MRI scan with no trouble at all. This page explains what to expect, so you can feel calm about the day.

## Before the day
!! If you have a pacemaker, a cochlear implant, an aneurysm clip or any other metal implant, call the imaging desk on extension 2210 at least 2 weeks before your scan. Some devices need special planning, and it can mean rescheduling.

- Tell us if you might be pregnant or have kidney disease.
- If you are uncomfortable in small spaces, ask your doctor about a mild sedative. If you take one, arrange a driver.
- If your scan uses contrast dye, do not eat for 4 hours before. You can drink water.

## On the day
- Arrive 30 minutes early at the Imaging Department on level 2.
- Bring a photo ID, your insurance details, and the referral if you were given a paper one.
- Leave jewelry, watches, hearing aids and wallets in the locker.
- Wear clothes without metal zippers or underwire.

## During the scan
Your scan takes 30 to 60 minutes. You lie on a padded bed that slides into a tube open at both ends.

The machine is loud, so we give you earplugs or headphones. You need to keep very still. You hold a squeeze ball that calls the technologist at any moment, so you are never alone.

## After the scan
- You can eat, drive and go back to work straight away, unless you took a sedative.
- If you had contrast, drink extra water.
- Your doctor receives the results within 3 business days. They appear in the patient portal after your doctor has seen them.
